index 000000000..cefc5de07
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/arm64/msm8996-c13.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,234 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+========================================
+Qualcomm MSM8996-based Readboy C13 tablet
+========================================
+
+The Readboy C13 (读书郎 C13) is a Chinese education tablet built around the
+Qualcomm Snapdragon 820 (MSM8996 v3) SoC with a PM8994 + PMI8996 PMIC pair.
+
+Hardware summary
+================
+
+- SoC: MSM8996 v3 (Kryo 2x2.15 GHz + 2x1.6 GHz), Adreno 530 GPU
+- RAM: 6 GB LPDDR4 (device-verified), eMMC 128 GB (C13_Y45_128G)
+- PMIC: PM8994 + PMI8996 (SMBCHG charger, FG fuel gauge, WLED backlight)
+- Display: 10.1" 1200x1920 DSI video-mode panel, 60 Hz, 4 lanes
+  - Two panel variants (selected by hardware revision):
+    - ``lmi_bn_1051``: Ilitek ILI9881D-class controller
+      (VERIFIED on this unit: ``mdss_mdp.panel=...lmi_bn_1051_video``)
+    - ``rk_bn_1051``: Himax-class controller
+  - Backlight: PMI8996 WLED; power: vddio 1.8 V + PMI8996 LAB/IBB bias
+- Touch: Himax HX83102E via the "HX common" driver (BLSP1 QUP5 SPI,
+  CS1=GPIO83, IRQ=GPIO125, RST=GPIO89) - VERIFIED on this unit via dmesg
+  ("himax_hx83102e_reg_re_init", RX=48 TX=32, 1200x1920).
+  Other variants in the stock DT: FocalTech FTS (BLSP2 QUP6 I2C 0x38),
+  Novatek NVT-ts-spi (BLSP1 QUP5 SPI CS0), Goodix GT9110 (I2C)
+- Battery: ~8000 mAh, 4.35 V max charge voltage, 3 A charge current
+  (profiles ``HTT_8000mah`` / ``ATL_7600mah`` from the stock device tree)
+- Sensors: Allegro ALS31300 3D hall sensor (I2C 0x60, IRQ=GPIO117),
+  AKM AK09970 magnetometer (I2C 0x11) - no accelerometer/gyro populated
+- Wireless: QCA6174 combo (WLAN on PCIe0, BT on BLSP1 UART2, reset=PMIC GPIO19)
+- Audio: WCD9335 (tasha) codec on SLIMbus, dual AW smart amps (AW8898/AW8811)
+- Storage: eMMC (SDHCI1, HS400), microSD (SDHCI2, CD=GPIO95)
+- USB: USB2-only Type-C (TUSB320 CC controller on BLSP2 QUP1 I2C 0x61),
+  SMB1351 secondary charger on the same bus
+- Cameras: 3x with autofocus actuators on CCI
+- Misc: DSPG DBMD8 voice DSP (BLSP1 QUP1 SPI), at24c32 EEPROM
+  (BLSP1 QUP6 I2C 0x51), PMI8996 haptics
+
+Board file
+==========
+
+``arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-readboy-c13.dts``
+
+The board wiring was derived from the stock boot.img device tree
+(Android 7.1.2 / kernel 3.18.31-perf, fingerprint
+``readboy/msm8996/msm8996:7.1.2/N2G47H/...``). GPIO numbers, I2C/SPI bus
+assignments, regulator voltages and panel command sequences were transcribed
+from that tree.
+
+Kernel changes in this port
+===========================
+
+- ``arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-readboy-c13.dts`` - the board file
+- ``arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996.dtsi`` - added ``blsp1_spi5`` (Himax SPI
+  touch) plus its pinctrl states (GPIO 81-84)
+- ``drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-readboy-c13.c`` - DSI panel driver with both
+  panel variants; on/off command sequences replayed verbatim from the stock
+  device tree (vendor DSI packet format: type, flags, vc, ack, wait_ms, len,
+  payload)
+- ``drivers/regulator/qcom-labibb-regulator.c`` - added the
+  ``qcom,pmi8996-lab-ibb`` compatible (PMI8996 LAB/IBB use the same SPMI
+  register map as PMI8998)
+- ``arch/arm64/configs/msm8996-c13.fragment`` - config fragment on top of the
+  arm64 ``defconfig``; merged into ``msm8996_readboy_c13_defconfig``
+
+Build
+=====
+
+::
+
+  # cross toolchain (any aarch64 gcc >= 5.1 or clang works)
+  export ARCH=arm64
+  export CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu-
+  make msm8996_readboy_c13_defconfig
+  make -j$(nproc) Image.gz-dtb dtbs modules
+
+Outputs: ``arch/arm64/boot/Image.gz-dtb`` (kernel + appended C13 DTB) and
+``arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-readboy-c13.dtb``.
+
+Flashing
+========
+
+Repack a boot image with the stock header parameters (base 0x80000000,
+kernel offset 0x8000, ramdisk offset 0x1000000, tags offset 0x100, page size
+4096, header v0, DTB appended to the kernel) - see ``make-bootimg.sh`` in the
+port directory. Flash to the ``boot`` partition with fastboot or TWRP::
+
+  fastboot flash boot boot-c13-mainline.img
+
+Console
+=======
+
+The console UART is BLSP2 UART2 (``serial1``, ``ttyMSM1``), which the stock
+bootloader addressed as ``ttyHSL0``. ``chosen/stdout-path`` points at it.
+
+Peripheral support status
+=========================
+
+=========================== ===================================================
+Peripheral                  Mainline status
+=========================== ===================================================
+Serial console              Working (blsp2_uart2)
+eMMC (sdhc1)                Working (HS400/HS200/8-bit)
+microSD (sdhc2)             Working
+USB2 (dwc3 + qusb2 phy)     Working; TUSB320 extcon for role detection
+PM8994/PMI8996 regulators   Working (rpm-smd + spmi regulators)
+PMI8996 charger/fuel gauge  Working (pmi8994_smbchg/pmi8994_fg compatibles)
+PMI8996 WLED backlight      Working (pmi8994_wled)
+PMI8996 LAB/IBB              Added ``qcom,pmi8996-lab-ibb`` (register-compatible
+                            with PMI8998; needs on-device verification)
+Display (DSI panel)         Driver present for both panel variants; the panel
+                            used on a given unit must be selected in DT
+                            (``readboy,lmi-bn1051`` vs ``readboy,rk-bn1051``).
+                            Needs on-device bring-up (timing flags, backlight).
+                            DRM core is built as modules in the shipped config
+                            (upstream behaviour), so an initramfs with modules
+                            is needed for display before rootfs mount.
+Bluetooth (QCA6174)         Working via ``qcom,qca6174-bt`` (hci_qca) on
+                            blsp1_uart2 - needs QCA6174 BT firmware
+WLAN (QCA6174)              PCIe0 RC enabled; QCA6174 should enumerate for
+                            ath10k. Needs ath10k firmware + board data,
+                            possibly the device-specific board-2.bin from the
+                            stock system. Not yet validated on hardware.
+Audio (WCD9335)             Codec wired on SLIMbus; machine driver
+                            (SND_SOC_MSM8996) available. Needs ADSP firmware.
+                            AW smart amps (AW8898/AW8811) have no mainline
+                            driver - speakers/headphones need a backport.
+Touch (Himax HX83102E)      Verified on device (SPI5/CS1). No mainline driver
+                            yet - backport the vendor ``hxcommon`` driver
+                            (supports hx83102e); DT node already in the board
+                            file. FocalTech/Novatek/Goodix nodes kept for the
+                            other hardware variants.
+ALS31300 hall sensor        Working (CONFIG_ALS31300)
+AK09970 magnetometer        No mainline driver yet (DT node kept for docs)
+Cameras (3x + AF)           Not in mainline (vendor qcom camera stack needed)
+SMB1351 secondary charger   Not in mainline (charging works via primary
+                            SMBCHG; parallel charging needs a backport)
+DSPG DBMD8 voice DSP        Not in mainline
+PMI8996 haptics             Working (qcom,spmi-haptics)
+=========================== ===================================================
+
+Firmware requirements
+=====================
+
+All firmware was extracted from the device itself (via TWRP adb) into the
+``firmware/`` directory next to this port. Stock firmware versions
+(``/modem/verinfo/ver_info.txt``):
+
+- ADSP: ``ADSP.8996.2.7.1.c3``, SLPI: ``SLPI.HB.1.0``, Modem: ``MPSS.TH.2.0.1.c8``
+- Video: ``VIDEO.VE.4.2``, CPE: ``CPE.TSF.1.0``, BT: ``BTFM.RM.4.3.c3``
+- RPM: ``RPM.BF.1.6``, TZ: ``TZ.BF.4.0.1``, ABL: ``BOOT.XF.1.0-00324``
+
+For a mainline userspace, install the extracted firmware into
+``/lib/firmware/`` on the rootfs. The Qualcomm PIL loaders (qcom_mdt_loader)
+support both ``.mbn`` and split ``.mdt``/``.bXX`` formats, so the files from
+the stock ``modem`` partition can be used as-is:
+
+ADSP / SLPI / venus / modem (from the stock ``modem`` partition, FAT32,
+``/image/`` - extracted to ``firmware/qcom-pil/``)::
+
+  adsp.mdt adsp.b00..b09
+  slpi.mdt slpi.b00..b14
+  venus.mdt venus.b00..b04
+  modem.mdt modem.b00..b20  mba.mbn
+  cpe_9335.mdt cpe_9335.bXX   (WCD9335 CPE, for audio wakeup)
+
+  -> copy to /lib/firmware/ (or /lib/firmware/qcom/msm8996/ and set the
+     DT "firmware-name" property accordingly)
+
+GPU (Adreno 530, from ``/system/etc/firmware/``, in ``firmware/gpu-adreno/``)::
+
+  a530_pfp.fw a530_pm4.fw a530_gpmu.fw2 a530v1_pm4.fw a530v2_seq.fw2
+  a530v3_gpmu.fw2 a530v3_seq.fw2 a530_zap.mdt a530_zap.b00..b02
+
+  -> /lib/firmware/qcom/a530* (zap is required for SMMU/GPU power-up)
+
+WLAN (QCA6174): the stock CLD firmware lives in ``firmware/qcom-pil/``
+(``qwlan30.bin``, ``bdwlan30.bin``, ``otp30.bin``, ``utf30.bin``,
+``data.msc``) plus ``firmware/wlan-qca6174/WCNSS_qcom_cfg.ini`` and
+``firmware/wlan_mac.bin`` (from ``persist``). ath10k needs its own layout
+under ``/lib/firmware/ath10k/QCA6174/hw3.0/``:
+
+- prefer the generic ``firmware-5.bin``/``board-2.bin`` from linux-firmware;
+- if RF does not work, try ``qwlan30.bin`` renamed to ``firmware-5.bin`` and
+  ``bdwlan30.bin`` renamed to ``board.bin`` (ath10k supports the legacy
+  board.bin layout; board-2.bin can be built with ``ath10k/ath10k-bdencoder``
+  if needed).
+
+Bluetooth (QCA6174): two equivalent sets exist:
+- ``firmware/bt-qca6174/`` (from the stock ``bluetooth`` partition):
+  ``btfw32.tlv`` + ``btnv32.bin`` (CLD names)
+- ``firmware/bt-qca6174/system/`` (from ``/system/etc/firmware/``):
+  ``rampatch_tlv_*.tlv`` + ``nvm_tlv_*.bin`` - these are what mainline
+  hci_qca requests. Copy e.g.::
+
+  rampatch_tlv_3.2.tlv -> /lib/firmware/qca/rampatch_tlv_3.2.tlv
+  nvm_tlv_3.2.bin     -> /lib/firmware/qca/nvm_tlv_3.2.bin
+
+  (check dmesg for the exact name the driver requests; hci_qca derives it
+  from the chip's ROM version)
+
+Audio:
+- ``firmware/audio-wcd9335/wcd9320/`` - WCD9335 codec firmware
+  (``wcd9320_anc.bin``, ``wcd9320_mbhc.bin``, ``wcd9320_mad_audio.bin``)
+  -> /lib/firmware/wcd9320/ (used by the wcd9335 driver)
+- ``firmware/audio-amps/`` - AW8811/AW8898 smart amp DSP firmware
+  (``aw881xx_pid_01_*``, ``aw8898_*``) - needed by the (not yet mainline)
+  amp drivers
+- ``firmware/dspg-dbmd8/dbmd8_va_fw.bin`` - DSPG DBMD8 voice DSP firmware
+- ``firmware/persist-sensors/`` + ``firmware/aw_cali.bin`` - sensor hub
+  calibration and amp calibration data (copy to /persist equivalent)
+
+Camera:
+- ``firmware/camera/cpp_firmware_v1_12_0.fw`` - camera CPP firmware
+  (needed by the not-yet-mainline camera stack)
+
+Touch (``firmware/touch/``): Himax (``Himax_firmware*.bin``), Novatek
+(``novatek_ts_fw_spi.bin``) and Goodix (``goodix_firmware_gt9110*.bin``)
+firmware blobs are loaded by their respective (vendor, not-yet-mainline)
+drivers. The unit in hand runs the FocalTech FTS controller (i2c-12 @0x38);
+FTS firmware is flashed to the IC by the vendor driver.
+
+Recommended first boot
+======================
+
+1. Build with ``msm8996_readboy_c13_defconfig``.
+2. Flash the resulting boot.img (kernel + a minimal initramfs with the
+   ``drm``/``msm``/panel/regulator modules and a shell - e.g. a small
+   busybox initramfs) - the serial console will show the full boot log.
+3. Confirm eMMC (mmcblk0), USB (gadget/peripheral), regulators and UART.
+4. Bring up the display: verify the panel variant (lmi vs rk) on the unit,
+   adjust the panel node compatible and any timing flags, then load the
+   msm DRM modules.
